  "reviewer": "Codex /root, separate from expedition author /root/audit_plan_issues",
  "rationale": "Reviewed all seven extension files and all four existing-file diffs against the pre-extension freeze. Existing changes only add workspace/member dependency and a descriptor; no core, ABI, driver oracle, benchmark or runner change. The module depends only on conformance-contract; C implements the same variable 15..23-byte canonical sorted stampbook independently through frozen imports/exports, without canonical guest globals. State/lifecycle is distinct from Encounter and Policy, owns a non-Clone Vec and uses query plus contribution capabilities only. Reviewed matching range, count, history, order, overflow, residence, duplicate and publication-before-action semantics in Rust and C. Four real-composition lifecycle tests compare full snapshots, revisions, results, traces including nested callback returns and contributions; they cover sparse membership, transfer, reset, replay rejection, retirement/reinstallation, incarnation rejection, removal/unload and calls=4 partial publication with detach/attach reconciliation. Correctness report third-expedition-C5F25R9t/correctness.json.gz passes 51 host tests, 89 common/native-negative executions and four independent lifecycle tests with IDs [1,2,73]. Source hashes and freeze check independently verified. Author previously worked on the supervisor, so this is separate module/core authorship, not a blind external-consumer or human-independent SDK audit. Mock replay is not durability and partial effects are not rollback; custom STAMP has no dedicated preregistered performance workload. Existing strict driver Clippy failures drop_non_drop and large_enum_variant are retained, not silently fixed through the freeze. No production or comparative-backend performance conclusion is approved by this review.",
